<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Johnson asked for a same-day visit for low back pain that began two days ago while he was carrying boxes of books up a flight of stairs. The pain is across the low back, worse on the right, aching with spasms when he turns or rises from a chair, and does not go down either leg. He has no numbness, weakness, trouble passing urine or controlling his bowels, numbness in the groin, fever, weight loss, history of cancer, or steroid use. He has taken nothing for it. He wanted to know which pain medicines are safe with his sertraline, because he has read that some pain medicines do not mix with it. His tics have been more frequent with the pain and poor sleep. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Two days ago, lifting boxes of books</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Low back, worse on the right; no radiation</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>Two days</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Aching, with spasms on turning</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>6 of 10</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>Worse rising from a chair and in the morning</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>On sertraline 100 mg daily</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Better lying on his side; no medicine taken</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>No leg pain, numbness, weakness, bladder or bowel change, saddle numbness, fever, or weight loss</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

